  "runtimeScope": [
    "A counted partial kitchen note over several existing variants persists a byUnits proposal with countedScope cart signature, candidate indices, creation time and page.",
    "The existing option-distribution and remainder parsers resolve explicit per-row quantities and unique current attribute/note references. One per variant is accepted only when it covers the requested unit count exactly.",
    "Every capacity, complete distribution total, existing noted-unit count, conflicting note, full note length and line limit is checked before committing any split. Original attributes, notes and unrelated lines are preserved.",
    "Counted choice pages retain global row numbers within WhatsApp limits. Totals, serialized sessions, stale cart/expiry, cancellation, repeated original requests and closure are covered.",
    "An otherwise valid implicit relative decrement whose product also exists in the current cart persists a purchaseScope question. Yes/de las pendientes resolves only the proposed purchase, and no/cancelar esta reducción discards only that reduction question.",
    "Numeric rows and confirmar cannot select the old owner while the scope question is active. Unrelated purchase revisions preserve the question, same-product absolute revisions supersede it, and a second ambiguous reduction cannot overwrite it.",
    "Legacy pending note/session fields remain optional. A previous scope guard contract was updated to require the new question while preserving the same original cart and proposed purchases."
  ],
  "developmentFindings": [
    "All four initial normal-entry cases failed because partial notes and ambiguous decrement answers lacked persisted continuation state.",
    "The existing byUnits note workflow and parsers were reused, with a scoped stale guard and exact per-variant allocation. Existing note clauses are counted so repeating the original instruction cannot create another unresolved distribution.",
    "An unrelated purchase revision could otherwise discard the active reduction question. Revised product IDs now distinguish an unrelated revision from a superseding same-product instruction.",
    "The active scope question has priority over the old numeric owner list and final confirmation. Explicit whole-order/whole-plan cancellation retains its existing meaning.",
    "The full inventory found two obsolete wording assertions in one legacy suite. The preserved-cart check passed. Those assertions now verify the partial distribution question, quantity, byUnits state and original cart signature. The complete 40-test suite was rerun. All other source hashes, including runtime sources, match the full run."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Provider responses, maps, persistence, Meta and order creation are simulated. Real-model wording and representative pilot results require additional measurement.",
    "The counted distribution covers a declared unit total of one SKU and its current variants. Partial quantities must be complete, uniquely owned and within each row capacity.",
    "Kitchen-note allocation uses explicit row/variant references, one-per-variant and the supported final remainder grammar. Other regional shorthand and mixed purchase/correction clauses require clarification.",
    "Scope confirmation resolves a proposed purchase reduction. A reply requesting an independent current-cart change while another complete edit plan remains held still requires broader cross-tool recovery.",
    "Several simultaneous ambiguous relative reductions are handled one active question at a time.",
    "Production promotion and generic Kamppo adaptation remain pending."
  ],
